      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T12:19:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is different logic than I\u0027m currently assuming/documenting. I would have assumed that a8/gray8/r8 gainmaps would be single channel and would therefore ignore the g/b of the gamma \u0026 ratio.\n\nIs a gray8 \"3-channel\" gainmap a thing? The math all works, but it doesn\u0027t make conceptual sense to me. If this is the case I need to go update the docs that say b/g are ignored to instead say \"must be equal to r\".\n\nIf it doesn\u0027t make sense, then gainmapIsRed isn\u0027t necessary since single channel only samples from r anyway.",
      "revId": "6bd9ef3ac24013771828d9a0310873f9c6173bae",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96a69b79_4e095e12",
