      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T12:29:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From my reading of the spec, it\u0027s legal to have a single channel gainmap where some of the per-channel parameters are different. It\u0027s ridiculous, but it\u0027s legal.\n\nSo I\u0027m requiring that all r,g,b components always be set. (It also feels easier to me -- the same SkGainmapInfo is valid for a color and non-color version of the same file).",
      "parentUuid": "59b4e8b8_6d5037cb",
      "revId": "6bd9ef3ac24013771828d9a0310873f9c6173bae",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
